 "notes": "Generated-row sibling (#4507) of genapp-lgipdb01: CUSTOMER, POLICY and the ENDOWMENT / HOUSE / MOTOR / COMMERCIAL type tables are generated from base/cntl/db2cre.jcl (the same generate block as genapp-lgapdb01-generated: identity policy numbers 1000001..1000012, FKs POLICY->CUSTOMER and type->POLICY, NULLs and boundary values), not GenApp's INSERTs. The 32 generated requests are written against those rows (a request names a customer and a policy that the seed 4507 rows hold, or one they do not): 01IEND / 01IHOU / 01IMOT / 01ICOM found, wrong customer (+100 '01'), policy of another type (+100); 02ICOM by policy; 03ICOM Cust_Cursor (customer 1 holds two commercial policies, which the hand-seeded case never reached: the cursor loop runs twice), a customer with one and one with none; 05ICOM Zip_Cursor (a postcode held, one it does not, one in the wrong case); 04ICOM and 99XXXX are unknown request ids ('99'). A change to the generator's draw moves which policies exist: the E2E test in tests/cobol_mainframe/test_equivalence_db2_rows.py fails the case then (the SQLCODE mix and row counts it asserts move). Not generated: an endowment inquiry on policy 1000010, whose generated PADDINGDATA is empty (not NULL): CA-E-PADDING-DATA(1:0) is a zero-length reference modification (oracle_assumptions.md X8, libcob 'length out of bounds: 0'), the endowment path lgapdb01-generated leaves out too. The error paths (a negative SQLCODE on a SELECT, an OPEN or a CLOSE, the short COMMAREA '98') are genapp-lgipdb01's. Program, LINKed LGSTSQ and the LGCMAREA COMMAREA as in genapp-lgipdb01. Seed additions (#6072): two more ENDOWMENT rows (policy 1000009, whose BROKERID is NULL, with a short padding; policy 1000011, whose PAYMENT is NULL, with NULL PADDINGDATA), a HOUSE row on policy 1000009 (NULL BROKERID) and a non-NULL MAKE on the MOTOR row of policy 1000011 and a non-NULL EQUITIES / WITHPROFITS on the two added ENDOWMENT rows (the generated NULL in those columns has no indicator, so such a row only ever answered -305 and never reached the NULL BROKERID / PAYMENT tests): they take the NULL-indicator outcomes at l.383, 397, 400, 410, 494 and 591 that the first draw never reached.",
